    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.colors\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.10.x\n\n### Description\n\nI'm currently testing out `mini.colors` and I noticed that `oklch(20 0.011368 253.09)` is getting incorrectly converted to `#2e2e2e`, when it should be `#12161c` ([oklch (switch to hex display)](https://oklch.com/#20,0.01368,253.09,100), firefox (see attached images))\n\n![Before](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/12e4b2ac-9b2a-402d-a68a-33e60b5bf002)\n![After](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8721ea2b-caf8-4efa-ad6a-555a67d1d74e)\n\n### Reproduction\n\n1. Run `:lua vim.notify(require(\"mini.colors\").convert({ l = 20, c = 0.01368, h = 253.09 }, \"hex\"))\n`\n\n2. Notification value is #2e2e2e",
