            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\n\nI am not aware about what algorithm the reference site uses. 'mini.colors' is based on the [algorithm and color picker](https://bottosson.github.io/misc/colorpicker/) written by the OKLch author. The module has intentional small deviations for performance (usually visible at the \"surface\" of maximum saturation/chroma for fixed lightness-hue), but otherwise it is pretty much consistent with its reference. The OKLch value for `#12161c` in both 'mini.colors' and its reference picker is [`{ l = 9.8 c = 1.36, h = 258.4 }`](https://bottosson.github.io/misc/colorpicker/#12161c).\n\nOne thing I noticed from a quick look at https://oklch.com, is that chroma normalization seems to be different: 'mini.colors' uses [positive integers](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/f40da50a3dfbbc53e6173beef8dc28626e1b5ebc/doc/mini-colors.txt#L206) while the oklch.com has values below 1.\n\nClosing as working as expected.",
