        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Latest `main` now has `convert` with [`adjust_lightness` option](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/307221b90376b68fc7e007e9315836370e9efb8f/doc/mini-colors.txt#L802-L807). Set it to `false` to disable this adjustment and make conversion more compatible with other Oklab/Oklch implementations. Together with [adjusted normalization](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/307221b90376b68fc7e007e9315836370e9efb8f/doc/mini-colors.txt#L225-L229), this should now provide results that are described in the issue.\n\nFor example, `:=require(\"mini.colors\").convert({ l = 20, c = 0.01368 * 100, h = 253.09 }, \"hex\", { adjust_lightness = false })` indeed results into `'#12161c'`.",
